abstract: "Code and data for a penalty-method analysis of soft boundary conditions in physics-informed neural networks. In the fixed-feature or tangent-kernel regime the boundary violation of the penalized minimizer equals (N + lambda I)^{-1} y*, is bracketed by rho/(lambda+nu) <= leak <= rho/lambda at every weight, and its product with the condition number tends to rho sigma_B^2 / mu. Trained tanh PINNs, a physics-informed DeepONet, and GPU-trained 3D networks confirm the predicted conditioning valley and the advantage of hard trial spaces, multiplier updates, and consistent boundary penalties."
